# .dockerignore — keep the Docker build context small.
#
# The Dockerfile only needs `src-rust/` (the Cargo workspace) to produce
# the `claude` binary. Everything else in the repo is either:
#   * spec text and reference material (spec/, public/, test/),
#   * deployment scripts that run *outside* the image (deploy/),
#   * local cargo build artefacts that would invalidate cache mounts
#     and balloon the build context (src-rust/target/),
#   * Git internals (.git/),
#   * editor/IDE droppings.
#
# Excluding them here speeds up `docker build` (less to upload to the
# daemon) and prevents cache-busting from unrelated file changes.

# --- VCS ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Editor / IDE ---
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
*.iml

# --- OS droppings ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Rust build artefacts ---
# `target/` is enormous and would invalidate the cargo build cache
# inside the image on every `docker build`. The cache mounts in the
# Dockerfile recreate cargo's cache on demand.
src-rust/target
**/target
**/*.rs.bk

# --- Spec / reference content not needed at runtime ---
spec
public
test

# --- Deployment scripts (run on the operator's machine, not in image) ---
deploy

# --- Local CLI / dev configuration (host-only, not for the image) ---
# `.claude/` carries `settings.json` + `settings.local.json` that pin the
# local CLI at DeepSeek's endpoint with a host-side API key — never ship.
# `litellm.yaml` is the LiteLLM proxy config used for local dev only.
# `CLAUDE.md` is repo orientation prose for humans, not runtime data.
.claude
litellm.yaml
CLAUDE.md
README.md
*.md

# --- Misc local-only files ---
*.log
*.tmp
.env
.env.*
node_modules

# --- Existing Dockerfile / dockerignore (no need to ship) ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
